concepts.text:
Absorption and reflection depend on wavelength. Some materials opaque to visible light transmit a fraction of X-rays or $\gamma$ rays, but transmission still depends on the material, its thickness, and photon energy.
Short-wavelength radiation is not unabsorbed by all matter. **Energy and momentum transfers by individual photons are often more apparent at high frequencies**;
particle-like behavior is not exclusive to short wavelengths.
